add('cover','Build a research loop.<br>Then give it an agent.', '<div class="sub">A four-hour experiment in the Solar Forecasting Lab.</div><LabScene /><div class="bottom-note">Solar forecasting, experiment tracking, and agents that edit research code.</div>', 'We’ll build two small forecasts from real solar observations. First we’ll write and track the experiments ourselves. Then we’ll let a research agent propose changes to the image model’s code. The pixel lab is an illustration; the observations and recorded results come from the workshop dataset.','cover','0:00')
add('arrival','Your team has a promising result.', '<div class="quote">“The new model looks better.”<small>THE RESEARCH UPDATE · FICTIONAL SCENE</small></div><div class="two-col" style="margin-top:40px"><div><h2>You ask which run.</h2><p>Someone shares a screenshot.</p></div><div><h2>You ask which code.</h2><p>Someone shares a notebook called final.</p></div></div>'+note('There are four notebooks called final.'), 'Imagine a teammate says the new model is better, but can only find a screenshot and several notebooks called final. That’s our fictional opening. Ask the room what they would need before trusting or repeating the comparison.','', '0:01')
add('assignment','Forecast the next solar observation', '<p class="big">Use the observations we have now to predict what the instruments will measure later.</p><div class="step-path"><div><h2>Measurements</h2><p>Use one hour of X-ray readings to predict flux 30 minutes ahead.</p></div><div><h2>Images</h2><p>Use two solar images to predict the image one hour ahead.</p></div></div><div class="bottom-note">These small experiments use real observations. They are not operational forecasts.</div>', 'Our first task uses the last hour of GOES X-ray measurements to predict flux thirty minutes later. The second uses two AIA images to predict another image one hour ahead. SunPy helps us inspect the observation times, wavelength, and units.','', '0:02')
add('research-question','Can an agent improve the research code?', '<div class="quote">“Once the experiment works, could an agent improve it?”<small>THE NEXT LAB QUESTION</small></div><ResearchMap :level="4" />', 'Once we can run and compare an experiment, we can give an agent the code and ask it to propose a change. We’ll train the small forecasting models as usual. The language model writing those proposals stays fixed.','', '0:03')
add('path','Build a forecast, then test changes to its code', '<div class="step-path"><div><h2>Forecast</h2><p>Load observations and write a baseline.</p></div><div><h2>Track</h2><p>Save code, settings, weights, and predictions.</p></div><div><h2>Improve</h2><p>Review and test the agent’s code changes.</p></div><div><h2>Evaluate</h2><p>Compare the selected models on later dates.</p></div></div><div class="bottom-note">You’ll edit Python in your own notebook and publish the results to your project.</div>', 'Follow this sequence in the notebook. You’ll change Python, run a check, execute the experiment, and open the resulting evidence in Forge. A change that fails to improve the forecast is still something we can investigate.','', '0:04')
add('copy','Copy the notebook into your Forge project', f'<div class="copy-layout"><div class="template-qr"><a href="{TEMPLATE}"><img src="/images/solar-template-qr.svg" alt="QR code opening the Solar workshop template"></a><p><a href="{TEMPLATE}">Open the Solar template ↗</a></p></div><ol><li>Open the template.</li><li>Choose <strong>Copy to project</strong> and select your writable project.</li><li>Open the copy in <strong>Edit</strong>. Choose <strong>Run all stale cells</strong> once.</li><li>In <strong>Connect</strong>, check your project. Exercise run buttons stay unpressed.</li></ol></div>'+note('Hosted Forge supplies authentication. Your account supplies notebook compute and inference access.'), 'Allow participants to get their own copy open before continuing. Run all stale cells creates the controls; it does not press the exercise run buttons. Hosted Forge supplies authentication, but attendees still need their own project and account access. Use fictional or public teaching data in a public project.', '', '0:05')
add('local','Run the same notebook on your laptop', code('git clone https://github.com/ash0ts/forge-workshop-kit.git\ncd forge-workshop-kit\nuv sync --frozen --extra solar\nuv run --extra solar wandb login --verify\nuv run --extra solar marimo edit notebooks/solar_autoresearch.py','sh')+'<p class="aside">In Connect, enter <code>your-entity/your-project</code>. Keep the terminal open.</p>'+note('Install Git and uv first. Hosted participants skip these commands.'), 'Hosted participants can skip this slide. On a laptop, install Git and uv, clone the repository, and run these commands. Authenticate in the terminal and keep that terminal open while marimo runs. There is no extra workshop service to start.','', '0:06')
add('settings','Check the compute and inference settings', '<table class="clean-table"><tr><th>Setting</th><th>This workshop</th></tr><tr><td>Project and credentials</td><td>Your own Forge project and account</td></tr><tr><td>Training compute</td><td>Notebook CPU; billed separately if hosted</td></tr><tr><td>Research agent</td><td><code>zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash</code>, fixed</td></tr><tr><td>Inference allowance</td><td>$8 by default; adjustable in Connect</td></tr><tr><td>Execution</td><td>Explicit run buttons; saved work restores</td></tr></table>'+note('A higher allowance permits more calls. It does not grant account access or include compute.'), 'Check these settings before running anything. The eight-dollar allowance applies to inference, while hosted notebook compute is separate. The research agent uses GLM-5.3-Flash with temperature 0.2, JSON output, and up to 16,384 output tokens. If that model is unavailable, stop and inspect the error rather than changing models mid-comparison.', '', '0:06')
add('trace-scopes','Record a tool call in Agent Lens', code('with tracing.Conversation(conversation_id=execution_id):\n    with tracing.Turn(agent_name="researcher", messages=mission):\n        with tracing.Tool(\n            name="inspect_training_environment",\n            arguments={}, result=observed_environment,\n        ):\n            ...')+note('Record the tool’s inputs, result, timing, and any error.'), 'A conversation groups the work. A turn records a request, and a tool span records one operation and its result. The notebook supplies the outer scopes. You’ll edit the tool scope and add an attribute you can then find in Agent Lens.','', '0:07')
turn('setup-turn','Connect and inspect your first tool call','Open <strong>1 · Connect</strong>.',['Click <strong>Connect and restore my work</strong>. Check that the project is yours.', 'In <code>instrument_tool</code>, add the <code>workshop.exercise</code> attribute with value <code>solar-research</code>. Click <strong>Check my tracing code</strong>.', 'Click <strong>Send my first Agent Lens trace</strong>. Open the tool call in Agent Lens and find the attribute you added.'],'Find your attribute beside the tool’s arguments and result.','Allow 7 minutes. Ask participants to show the attribute they added in their own Agent Lens tool call. The setup operation inspects the notebook environment and makes no language-model request. If someone cannot publish it, check project access before proceeding.','0:08–0:15','answer-trace')
add('setup-screen','Check the project before you run an exercise', '<div class="native-columns"><a href="/images/ux-v022-solar-setup.png" target="_blank"><img src="/images/ux-v022-solar-setup.png" alt="Revised notebook showing the participant project, allowance and guided exercise navigation"></a><div><h2>Check your project.</h2><p>Enter the Forge project where you want to save this workshop.</p><h2>Check your allowance.</h2><p>Inference and notebook compute are separate.</p><p class="aside"><a href="/images/ux-v022-solar-setup.png" target="_blank">Open full capture ↗</a></p></div></div>'+note('The setup screen before connecting to a project.'), 'This screenshot shows the Connect step before access is checked. Enter your own project, choose an inference allowance, then click Connect and restore my work. This image does not show a completed connection.', '', '0:15')
add('instrumentation-screen','Add an attribute to the tool span', '<div><a class="instrumentation-crop" href="/images/ux-v020-solar-instrumentation.png" target="_blank" aria-label="Open the full tracing exercise"><img src="/images/ux-v020-solar-instrumentation.png" alt="Actual editable instrument_tool function with the attribute exercise and free tracing check"></a><p class="aside">Add the attribute inside the tool scope. This writer also instruments your later training calls.</p><div class="image-caption">Recorded rehearsal: the attribute is added and the local check passes. <a href="/images/ux-v020-solar-instrumentation.png" target="_blank">Open full capture ↗</a></div></div>', 'Point to the attribute inside the tool scope. The free code check tests the function locally. The separate trace button publishes the environment check. This same function will record later training calls.', '', '0:15')
add('goes-window','Predict X-ray flux 30 minutes ahead', '<ForecastWindow mode="goes" />'+note('Predict log10 XRS-B flux. A forecast window includes observations, timestamps, and a future target.'), 'Read the timeline from left to right. The model gets sixty minutes of observed flux, then predicts the reading thirty minutes after now. We work in log10 flux, so the error is in transformed units rather than raw watts per square metre.','', '0:15')
add('chronology','Use earlier dates to train, later dates to test', '<ForecastWindow :split="true" />'+note('February 2014, UTC. Fit normalization on training data only.'), 'Train on February 1–10, choose models using February 11–12, and leave February 13–14 for the final comparison. Every input and the target of a window must belong to one partition. Fit normalization using training data only.','', '0:17')
add('gaps','Leave out windows with missing observations', '<div class="two-col"><div><h2>Check the timestamps</h2><p>The prepared GOES archive has no data for February 8.</p><p>A window needs its full input history and its future target.</p></div><div><h2>Skip an incomplete window</h2><p>Keep the missing date in the coverage record.</p><p>A zero would invent a measurement that the instrument never supplied.</p></div></div><div class="bottom-note">Use the same accepted windows for every model in the comparison.</div>', 'February 8 is absent from the prepared GOES source archive. A window that needs those readings cannot be used. Filling the absence with zero would tell the model that the instrument measured zero flux, which it did not.','', '0:19')
add('sunpy','Inspect a solar observation with SunPy', code('from sunpy.map import Map\n\nobservation = Map(dataset_path / "sample-aia.fits")\nprint(observation.date)\nprint(observation.wavelength)\nprint(observation.unit)')+note('Inspect the FITS metadata here; use the prepared arrays for training.'), 'Open the representative FITS file and inspect its date, wavelength, and unit. Training uses prepared arrays so the class does not wait for archive downloads. The dataset includes the acquisition and preprocessing records, so we can trace those arrays back to the public observations.','', '0:20')
turn('data-turn','Inspect the observations before training','Open <strong>2 · Solar data</strong>.',['Click <strong>Load the solar dataset</strong>.', 'In the data preview, find an observation time, the image wavelength, and the train/validation/test dates.', 'Use the date diagram to explain why a window with inputs on February 10 and a target on February 11 would be excluded.'],'You can say what the model receives and which future observation it must predict.','Give participants six minutes. Have them explain one forecast window to a neighbor: which observations go in, which observation is the target, and which dates it belongs to. No training is needed yet.','0:21–0:27')
add('persistence','Start by copying the latest reading', code('def persistence_forecast(split):\n    # Latest observed value becomes the future prediction.\n    ...')+'<p class="big">Predict flux 30 minutes ahead by copying the latest reading.</p>'+note('This uses only a reading we already have. It does not look at the future target.'), 'Persistence means predicting that the latest value will stay the same. Solar observations are correlated over time, so this simple baseline can be hard to beat. It gives us a comparison before we spend time training a network.','', '0:27')
add('metric','Measure how far the prediction missed', code('error = mean(abs(predicted_log_flux - observed_log_flux))')+'<div class="two-col" style="margin-top:35px"><div><h2>Lower is better</h2><p>The same target, transform, and units apply to every run.</p></div><div><h2>Look at individual misses</h2><p>Inspect the times where the forecast misses.</p></div></div>'+note('Compare each prediction with the observed future, then average the errors.'), 'For each forecast, subtract the observed log-flux target, take the absolute error, then average across windows. Lower is better. The average can hide a bad interval, so we also inspect the curves. Keep flux error separate from the later image score.','', '0:29')
turn('persistence-turn','Write and test persistence','Open <strong>3 · Persistence</strong>.',['Implement <code>persistence_forecast(split)</code>.','Click <strong>Check my persistence function</strong>, then <strong>Run my persistence baseline</strong>.','Inspect the observed and predicted curves. Identify one interval where copying the present misses the future.'],'The plot shows your persistence forecast beside the observed flux. Point to one miss.','Allow ten minutes. Let participants attempt the function before opening the answer. Ask them to find an interval where the real flux changed while persistence kept the previous value. That is a concrete error another model could try to reduce.','0:30–0:40','answer-persistence')
add('number','Save what changed between runs', '<p class="big">Suppose a second run has a lower validation error. What changed?</p><div class="step-path"><div><h2>Code</h2><p>You changed the loss function.</p></div><div><h2>Data</h2><p>You excluded an incomplete window.</p></div><div><h2>Settings</h2><p>You trained for more steps.</p></div></div><div class="bottom-note">Save these differences so someone else can repeat the comparison.</div>', 'Use these as possible explanations for a changed score, not claims about this rehearsal. If code, data, or training time differs, we need to know that before deciding why the score moved.','', '0:40')
add('run-inspector','Which setting changed between these runs?', '<RunInspector />', 'These are two recorded GOES runs. Before revealing the settings, ask what the scores let us conclude. Then click Show active settings. Both runs used the same source and budget, but their learning rates differed.', '', '0:41')
add('run-inspector-reveal','These runs used different learning rates', '<RunInspector :revealed="true" />', 'The learning rate changed from .001 to .003. Data, source, seed, steps, and batch size stayed the same. Both errors were worse than persistence, so choosing the smaller of these two errors still leaves a poor forecast.', '', '0:42')
add('program','Turn observations into a forecast', '<ResearchMap :level="0" />', 'Start with the forecast itself: observations enter the model and it produces a number or an image. We’ll add the records around this process one piece at a time.','', '0:42')
add('source','Save the model and training code with the run', '<ResearchMap :level="1" />'+note('Save the source used for this run before editing it for the next experiment.'), 'The model and training functions are code we can change. Save the particular source used by this run, because the notebook may be edited again tomorrow.','', '0:43')
add('independent','Use the same scoring rule for every model', '<ResearchMap :level="2" />'+note('The model can change. The target, partition, and primary scoring rule stay fixed.'), 'Keep the target, dates, and primary metric unchanged while comparing models. Otherwise a lower score might come from an easier test rather than a better forecast.','', '0:44')
add('record','Save the files needed to repeat the run', '<ResearchMap :level="3" /><div class="bottom-note">A W&B Artifact is a versioned bundle of files: here, data, code, trained weights, and predictions.</div>', 'A W&B run stores settings and metric history. A W&B Artifact stores a versioned bundle of files. Here that means the data, source, weights, and predictions needed to repeat or inspect a result.','', '0:45')
add('stage','Save code and outputs with each training run', code('with session.stage(\n    "measurement/run", config=config,\n    sources={"candidate.py": source},\n    inputs={"dataset": dataset_version, "split": "validation"},\n) as stage:\n    if stage.needs_run:\n        result = train_model(data, config)\n        stage.record(result)')+note('You write the training function. The session records its code and outputs.'), 'This shortened example shows where saving sits around training. The notebook’s run_training function runs your source, then saves the result. If that same stage has already completed, the saved result can be restored instead of training again.','', '0:47')
add('artifacts','Restore a completed run after a restart', '<div class="step-path"><div><h2>Finish a run</h2><p>Save its code, outputs, and completion record locally.</p></div><div><h2>Upload a checkpoint</h2><p>Store a versioned copy as a W&B Artifact in your project.</p></div><div><h2>Reopen the notebook</h2><p>Restore that checkpoint and inspect the completed results.</p></div></div><div class="bottom-note">You can continue from the saved run without training the model again.</div>', 'The local completion record tells the notebook which work finished. The checkpoint Artifact stores a copy in your project. If the runtime is replaced, restore the checkpoint before continuing. An upload failure can be retried using the local files.','', '0:49')
turn('tracking-turn','Write the loss and metric','Open <strong>4 · Track and search</strong>.',['Implement <code>training_loss</code> and <code>my_flux_mae</code>.', 'Click <strong>Check my measurement code</strong>. Test identical arrays and a constant one-unit error.', 'In <code>run_training</code>, find where it saves source, settings, weights, and predictions. The next exercise will produce those files.'],'Your checks pass, and you can point to where run_training saves its files.','Allow fifteen minutes. Have participants implement the loss and metric, run the small checks, then find the file-saving calls in run_training. The next exercise produces those files. If they struggle with the metric, use a prediction of one against a target of zero as the first example.','0:50–1:05','answer-flux')
add('search-levels','Choose settings, choose a model, or write new code', '<table class="clean-table"><tr><th>Operation</th><th>What changes</th></tr><tr><td>Hyperparameter search</td><td>Values used by an existing program</td></tr><tr><td>Architecture comparison</td><td>Which implemented model runs</td></tr><tr><td>Agent-directed research</td><td>The model, loss, or training program itself</td></tr></table>'+note('We will do all three. The first two do not require a research agent.'), 'Changing learning rate is a hyperparameter search. Choosing MLP or CNN compares existing architectures. Later, the research agent will write different model or training code. These are different kinds of changes, and we’ll record which one we made.','', '1:05')
add('configs','Compare six model configurations', '<table class="clean-table"><tr><th>Architecture</th><th>Widths</th><th>Learning rates</th><th>Training budget</th></tr><tr><td>Small MLP</td><td>16, 32, 16</td><td>.001, .001, .003</td><td>60 steps each</td></tr><tr><td>Temporal CNN</td><td>16, 32, 16</td><td>.001, .001, .003</td><td>60 steps each</td></tr></table>'+note('Seed 17. Batch size 32. The notebook records the active values.'), 'These six configurations are the workshop defaults: two model families, three settings per family, seed 17, batch size 32, and sixty training steps. It’s a short CPU exercise, so inspect whether the models have trained enough before drawing an architecture conclusion.','', '1:07')
add('sweep','Run the configurations through W&B Sweeps', code('sweep_id = wandb.sweep(sweep_config, entity=entity, project=project)\n\ndef trial():\n    with wandb.init() as run:\n        result = run_training(config_for(run.config.trial))\n        run.log(result["metrics"])\n\nwandb.agent(sweep_id, function=trial, count=6)')+note('The notebook contains the full implementation and reuses already-completed runs.'), 'W&B Sweeps assigns each configuration to a run. Our training function does the fitting and saves its outputs. This is a shortened excerpt; the notebook contains the entity, project, and complete configuration setup.','', '1:09')
add('native-sweep','Compare forecast error and training time', '<a class="sweep-crop" href="/images/ux-v020-solar-sweep.png" target="_blank" aria-label="Open the full native W&B Sweep capture"><img src="/images/ux-v020-solar-sweep.png" alt="Actual W&B Sweep charts showing six validation errors, negative skill relative to persistence, and runtime"></a><p class="aside">All six recorded forecasts are worse than persistence. A lower error among them does not change that.</p><div class="image-caption"><a href="https://forge.coreweave.com/wandb/wandb/forge-workshop-kit/sweeps/pr1xsoaw">Open the actual Sweep ↗</a> · <a href="/images/ux-v020-solar-sweep.png" target="_blank">Full capture ↗</a></div>', 'This is the recorded six-run Sweep. Find validation error, performance relative to persistence, and training time. All six models performed worse than persistence here. The lowest error among them does not make it a successful forecast.', '', '1:10')
add('learning-curve','Check whether the models learned enough', '<p class="big">Open the loss curve and prediction plot before choosing a model.</p><div class="warning">In our recorded GOES runs, 60 training steps left the models undertrained. Copying the latest reading gave lower error.</div><div class="bottom-note">Testing a longer training budget would be a separate comparison.</div>', 'In the recorded runs, the loss curves and forecasts showed the models were still undertrained after sixty steps. Compare that with the forecasts you just produced. A longer, equal training budget for all models would be a separate experiment.','', '1:11')
turn('search-turn','Run six configurations and inspect one forecast','Stay in <strong>4 · Track and search</strong>.',['Click <strong>Run six tracked configurations</strong>.', 'Open the Sweep. Compare validation error and training time for two configurations.', 'Open one run’s Artifact. Find its source and predictions, then compare the forecast with its loss curve and score.'],'Explain one comparison using the settings, curve, and forecast.','Allow fifteen minutes. Ask participants to predict which configuration will win before running the search. After it finishes, have them explain one result from the loss curve and forecast. Keep failed runs visible so the comparison accounts for what happened.','1:15–1:30','answer-search')
add('break','The experiments can wait ten minutes.', '<p class="big">Save your work and take ten minutes.<br>We’ll start the image experiment when we return.</p><div class="bottom-note">The notebook can stay open. There’s no exercise to run during the break.</div>', 'Take ten minutes. Confirm saved work is visible before leaving. No background experiment is required during the break.','', '1:30–1:40')
add('images-window','Predict the solar image one hour ahead', '<ForecastWindow mode="images" />'+note('AIA 171 Å. Prepared 64 × 64 arrays. One-hour forecasting.'), 'Now we give the model images from sixty minutes ago and now, and ask for the image sixty minutes ahead. The AIA 171 Å arrays are 64 by 64 pixels so the exercise can run on CPU.','', '1:40')
add('image-stack','Save image experiments the same way', '<ResearchMap :level="3" />'+note('The input and prediction changed shape. Source, settings, weights, and evidence still belong together. The image score uses normalized log1p intensity.'), 'The inputs are now images, but we still save the same kinds of records: data, code, settings, weights, and predictions. Image values use normalized log1p intensity, so their errors have a different scale from the GOES errors.','', '1:42')
add('persistence-image','Look at the forecast beside the observed future', pic('solar-validation.png','Recorded image input, prediction, future observation, and error','Recorded rehearsal image forecast. The notebook shows your own prediction after training.'), 'Read this recorded example from input to prediction, observed future, and error map. Ask someone to point to a region that changed. After training, the notebook will show the same view for their own result.','', '1:44')
add('conv','Have the network predict the whole image', code('class ImagePredictor(nn.Module):\n    def forward(self, x):\n        return self.net(x)')+'<p class="big">The convolutional model must produce the whole image.</p>'+note('Two input channels: the earlier and current images. One output channel: the forecast.'), 'The first model takes two image channels and predicts a whole future image. Its output has one channel. We keep the network small enough to compare on CPU during the workshop.','', '1:46')
add('residual','Add a learned correction to the current image', code('class ImagePredictor(nn.Module):\n    def forward(self, x):\n        correction = self.net(x)\n        return x[:, 1:2] + correction')+'<p class="big">The current image supplies a starting point. The network learns the change.</p>', 'The residual model adds its learned correction to the current image. If the correction is zero, its forecast is exactly persistence. Participants implement this branch in the same forward method.','', '1:48')
add('image-score','Measure error inside the solar disk', code('error = abs(prediction - target)\nmasked_error = error * disk_mask\nscore = mean(masked_error.sum_per_image() / disk_mask.sum_per_image())')+note('A change outside the mask must not affect the score. Test that explicitly.'), 'Compute absolute error only inside the fixed solar-disk mask. Sum and divide within each image, then average the image errors. An edit outside the mask should not change this score.','', '1:50')
add('loss','Train with one loss; compare with a fixed metric', '<table class="clean-table"><tr><th>Training loss</th><th>Primary evaluation metric</th></tr><tr><td>Supplies gradients while fitting weights</td><td>Measures predictions for comparison</td></tr><tr><td>Candidate code can change it</td><td>Fixed outside candidate code</td></tr><tr><td>The starting implementation uses squared error</td><td>The image comparison uses masked absolute error</td></tr></table>', 'The training loss supplies gradients that update weights. The evaluation metric tells us how the forecast compares with another model. We can try a different training loss while keeping the scoring rule fixed. That will be one of the agent’s recorded proposals.','', '1:52')
add('image-code-screen','Compare the two forecasts on the same case', '<a class="model-crop" href="/images/ux-v020-solar-models.png" target="_blank" aria-label="Open the complete validation model comparison"><img src="/images/ux-v020-solar-models.png" alt="Actual convolutional and residual forecasts on the same validation case, with observed future and error images"></a><div class="image-caption">Recorded validation case: convolution above, residual below. <a href="/images/ux-v020-solar-models.png" target="_blank">Open full comparison and evidence links ↗</a></div>', 'These two recorded rows use the same input and target times. The convolutional forecast is above; the residual forecast is below. Compare the images and error maps, then look at the validation scores. The final dates have not been used to select either model.', '', '1:54')
turn('image-turn','Implement and compare the image predictors','Open <strong>5 · Solar images</strong>.',['Edit <code>ImagePredictor.forward</code>, <code>training_loss</code>, and <code>my_image_mae</code>.','Click <strong>Check my image code</strong>. A +1 error should score 1; an off-disk change should score 0.','Click <strong>Compare convolutional and residual predictors</strong>. Inspect both forecasts.'],'Show which model validation selected, then point to a region where its forecast missed.','Give participants twenty minutes. Start with the local scorer examples, then train both model versions. Ask each participant to explain why validation selected one and show a region it still missed.','1:55–2:15','answer-images')
add('agent-need','Give the research agent your code and results', '<p class="agent-explanation">So far, you’ve written the models and chosen their settings. Now give a research agent that code and its validation results, and ask for two changes. Read the diffs, train both candidates, and compare their errors. The version selected by validation error becomes the starting point for the next round.</p><div class="bottom-note">The agent writes proposals. You review the code before the notebook runs it.</div>', 'Read this transition as one explanation. Until now, we wrote the models and chose the settings ourselves. We’ll now ask an agent for two code changes, inspect them, and use the experiment we built to test them. The selected code becomes the next round’s starting point.','', '2:15')
add('weights','The research agent writes code; the forecast model trains', '<table class="clean-table"><tr><th></th><th>Research agent</th><th>Forecasting model</th></tr><tr><td>Job</td><td>Propose code edits</td><td>Predict solar observations</td></tr><tr><td>Weights</td><td>Fixed throughout</td><td>Trained on training dates</td></tr><tr><td>Changed by this loop</td><td>Its evidence and task context</td><td>Source, loss, training code, trained weights</td></tr></table>'+note('No post-training of the research agent occurs in this workshop.'), 'There are two different models here. GLM writes research proposals and its weights stay fixed. The small forecasting networks train their weights for each candidate. The research agent changes the program that performs that training.','', '2:17')
add('boundaries','Decide which files the agent may change', '<div class="two-col"><div><h2>The agent may edit</h2><p>Model layers<br>Feature computation<br>Training loss<br>Training procedure</p></div><div><h2>The experiment keeps fixed</h2><p>Training and validation dates<br>What we predict<br>How we score predictions<br>The reserved final-test dates</p></div></div><div class="bottom-note">Candidate Python runs in this notebook’s environment after your review.</div>', 'The agent can edit feature, model, loss, and training code. It cannot change the date partitions, forecast target, or comparison metric. Review every proposed diff before execution. These training subprocesses are time-limited and do not inherit Forge credentials, but they are not a security sandbox.','', '2:19')
add('evidence','Send the code, settings, and validation results', '<div class="step-path"><div><h2>Exact source</h2><p>The files that produced the parent result.</p></div><div><h2>Active settings</h2><p>Architecture, steps, width, optimizer values.</p></div><div><h2>Validation evidence</h2><p>Curves, errors, predictions, and failed attempts.</p></div></div>'+note('A default in source may not be the value the run used.'), 'Send the files and settings that produced the current result, plus its validation outputs. A default learning rate in source may differ from the value used in the run. The agent needs the active values to propose a relevant change.','', '2:21')
add('agent-span','Follow the agent’s work in Agent Lens', '<div class="step-path"><div><h2>Open the request</h2><p>Read what we asked the agent to change.</p></div><div><h2>Inspect the tool calls</h2><p>Find the evidence it read and the code it returned.</p></div><div><h2>Follow the test</h2><p>Open the training call and look at its result or error.</p></div></div><div class="bottom-note">Compare the agent’s stated reason with what happened when its code ran.</div>', 'Open the research conversation in Agent Lens. Start with the mission, then find the evidence-reading tool and the returned code. Follow a training call to its result or error. Compare that sequence with the agent’s explanation of its change.','', '2:23')
add('native-lens','Find the validation evidence the agent read', screen('ux-v023-solar-lens.png', 'Native Agent Lens showing the research agent evidence-reading tool and its recorded output', 'Select read_validation_evidence. Find the settings and validation error.', TRACE+'/spans', 'Open the conversation', 'Recorded research-agent request. The tool output is the evidence supplied to the proposed edit.'), 'Open the evidence-reading tool and find the current source settings and validation result. Then inspect the returned proposal and follow its training result. This capture comes from the recorded rehearsal, not a new request. The full-size image remains available when sign-in is required.', '', '2:24')
turn('evidence-turn','Choose the evidence for the research agent','Open <strong>6 · Research agent</strong>.',['In <code>select_validation_evidence(record)</code>, keep the active settings and validation results. Click <strong>Check my evidence selection</strong>.', 'Read the check result. Confirm that the final-test example is rejected.', 'Name the validation fields your function will send to the agent. What can it learn from them?'],'You can name the code and validation results the agent will receive.','Allow twelve minutes. Participants should edit the evidence selector, then run the check that accepts validation evidence and rejects the final-test example. Ask them to name what the agent will receive before sending a request.','2:25–2:40','answer-evidence')
add('propose','Ask for two changes to the same starting code', '<ResearchBranches :level="1" />'+note('<a href="https://github.com/google-research/harness2/tree/1cfe254e8d25b15f37048c3730134686abe60335">Harness²-inspired</a>: our probes train forecasting weights and include validation scores.'), 'Both candidates start from the same code and settings. This borrows Propose–Probe–Compose from Harness². Here the probes train forecasting models and give validation scores to the editor, so it is a teaching adaptation rather than the paper’s exact task protocol.','', '2:40')
add('native-diff','Read the proposed change before running it', '<a class="diff-crop" href="/images/ux-v020-solar-diff.png" target="_blank" aria-label="Open the full proposed-change capture"><img src="/images/ux-v020-solar-diff.png" alt="Actual candidate diff changes squared training error to absolute error and requires review before the probe"></a><div class="image-caption">Recorded proposal: <code>.square()</code> became <code>.abs()</code>. The training result will show whether it helped. <a href="/images/ux-v020-solar-diff.png" target="_blank">Full capture ↗</a></div>', 'This recorded candidate changes squared training loss to absolute loss. Ask what that might change during training, then inspect the test result. Reading the diff tells us what was proposed; it does not tell us whether the forecast improved.', '', '2:41')
add('probe','Train and score each candidate', '<ResearchBranches :level="2" />'+note('Use the same training and validation data. Keep failed runs visible.'), 'Train each candidate on the same training dates and compare its validation error. If one fails before producing a forecast, inspect the error and leave its score missing.','', '2:42')
add('compose','Ask the agent which changes to keep', '<ResearchBranches :level="3" />'+note('The agent can keep A, keep B, combine changes, or retain the starting code.'), 'The agent reads both test results and can keep one candidate, combine changes, or retain the starting code. The dashed lines mean that it reviewed the results. They do not mean both sets of changes were merged.','', '2:44')
add('test-composed','Test the version the agent chose', '<ResearchBranches :level="4" />'+note('Run the selected code on the same training and validation dates.'), 'Run the chosen code before accepting it. Combining two changes can behave differently from either one alone. If the unchanged version is retained, testing it creates another execution of the same code.','', '2:46')
add('repeat','Start round two from the selected version', '<ResearchBranches :level="5" />'+note('Use the selected code and what the first tests showed to plan the next changes.'), 'The selected code and a short lesson enter round two. The agent now proposes changes on top of that version. We are still forecasting the same image task and selecting with the same validation metric.','', '2:48')
turn('round1-turn','Propose and test two changes','Inspect <code>next_research_action</code> in <strong>6 · Research agent</strong>.',['<strong>Propose two code changes</strong>. Read both diffs.','Confirm review of Candidate A → <strong>Test Candidate A</strong>. Confirm review of Candidate B → <strong>Test Candidate B</strong>.','<strong>Record my comparison</strong>, then <strong>Request a composition</strong>.'],'Each candidate’s proposal diff and training result are linked in Agent Lens.','Keep this slide visible while participants propose and test the first two candidates. Ask them to explain each diff before confirming review. After both tests, record a comparison and request the agent’s choice.','2:50–3:00')
turn('round2-turn','Test the selected code, then begin round two','Continue the same workbench.',['Confirm review of composition, then <strong>Test the composition</strong>.','Click <strong>Save the adopted version and lesson</strong>. Check whether the parent was retained.','Repeat the process in round two using the previous outcome.'],'Open the selected version from each round and explain why it was kept.','Give participants fifteen minutes for the tested selection and the second round. Retaining the previous code is a valid outcome. Ask why it was retained, then show its saved execution rather than treating KEEP as skipped work.','3:00–3:15','answer-controller')
add('branch-inspect','Follow one proposal through the branch diagram', '<ResearchBranches :level="5" :interactive="true" />', 'Click a candidate, its test, and the selection step. Ask someone to explain what happened along that path. This diagram explains the process; the notebook’s branch view opens their actual files and results.','', '3:15')
add('freeze','Stop editing before the final comparison', '<div class="step-path"><div><h2>Persistence</h2><p>Copy the latest observed image.</p></div><div><h2>Manual selection</h2><p>The model selected using validation error.</p></div><div><h2>Agent selection</h2><p>The code and weights selected after round two.</p></div></div>'+note('Keep these versions fixed while testing the reserved dates.'), 'Select the versions before looking at the final dates. The image comparison includes persistence, the manually selected model, and the agent-selected model. Keep the saved code and weights fixed while evaluating them.','', '3:17')
add('frozen-code','Load the saved weights to make final predictions', code('model = build_model(input_shape, frozen_config)\nmodel.load_state_dict(saved_weights)\nmodel.eval()\nwith torch.no_grad():\n    prediction = model(final_inputs)')+note('There is no optimizer step in this stage.'), 'Load the saved weights, switch to evaluation mode, and predict without an optimizer step. Final evaluation measures the selected trained model; it does not train another one.','', '3:19')
add('aligned','Compare predictions for the same times', '<table class="clean-table"><tr><th>Case identity</th><th>Persistence</th><th>Manual</th><th>Agent-selected</th></tr><tr><td>Same input timestamps</td><td>Prediction + error</td><td>Prediction + error</td><td>Prediction + error</td></tr><tr><td>Same target timestamp</td><td>Saved output</td><td>Executed source</td><td>Executed source</td></tr></table>'+note('Use each case ID to find the same input and target times in Weave or EvalTables.'), 'Choose one case identity and compare the predictions for its shared input and target times. Weave stores these evaluation records. Native EvalTables was unavailable during the rehearsal, so the notebook and Weave comparison remain available; publication can be retried separately.','', '3:21')
turn('final-turn','Test the selected models on reserved dates','Open <strong>7 · Final evaluation</strong>.',['Click <strong>Freeze versions and evaluate reserved dates</strong>.', 'Choose one timestamp. Compare each image forecast with the same observed future.', 'Open one result’s training record and Agent Lens call. Compare the image scores separately from the GOES scores.'],'Explain a difference between two forecasts using their images and scores.','Allow twenty minutes. Have participants choose one timestamp and explain a difference in the forecasts using the error images. Keep the GOES and image tables separate. Nearby windows overlap, so they are not independent studies.','3:25–3:45','answer-final')
add('result-meaning','Open the comparison in your project', screen('ux-v023-solar-dashboard.png', 'Native Solar workspace showing the three frozen image-model results', 'Compare the three image forecasts, then open a run for its time and cost.', SOLAR_WORKSPACE, 'Open the Solar workspace', 'Recorded rehearsal: image error fell; the GOES model lost to persistence. The metrics use different units.'), 'This saved workspace contains only the runs from one rehearsal. Compare final image scores, then inspect GOES separately. Open a run to see its settings, runtime, and evidence. Do not combine these two tasks into one average. The selected runs and source metrics are unchanged.', '', '3:48')
add('reproduce','Open the files behind one result', screen('ux-v023-solar-artifact.png', 'Native W&B Artifact file list for the selected round-two training execution', 'Open candidate.py, losses.json, predictions.npy, and weights.pt.', SOLAR_ARTIFACT, 'Open the Artifact', 'The selected round-two training run saved its code, losses, weights, and predictions together.'), 'Open the Artifact file list for round two’s tested composition. candidate.py is the executed code, losses.json records training, weights.pt holds trained parameters, and predictions.npy and predictions.png contain the output. execution.json links the settings and result. This is the saved training run whose weights were subsequently frozen, not a new execution.', '', '3:49')
turn('conclusion-turn','Write down what changed and whether it helped','Use your own comparison.',['Name one code change and report its error on the reserved dates.', 'Include a forecast that still missed. Say what you would try next.', 'Click <strong>Publish my conclusion</strong>. Follow a link in your Report back to the saved code or prediction.'],'Your conclusion names the change, the measured result, and a remaining problem.','Allow eight minutes. Ask participants to name a change, report what happened, and include a remaining miss. A negative result is fine. If publication fails, save the conclusion and retry the upload without rerunning the experiment.','3:50–3:58')
add('close','Explain the result, then choose the next experiment', screen('ux-v023-solar-report-results.png', 'Native Solar Report bar chart comparing the three frozen image forecasts', 'Name one code change, its measured result, and a remaining forecasting error.', REPORT, 'Open the recorded Report', 'For another study, choose new final-test dates before editing again.'), 'A teammate should be able to follow this explanation back to the run, source, and prediction. Ask for one next experiment based on an error someone inspected: what would change, what would stay fixed, and what would make them keep the previous version? This Report describes the recorded rehearsal; participants publish their own conclusions.', '', '3:58–4:00')
main_count=len(slides)
# Optional reference and recorded evidence. Never required to finish the exercise.
add('reference','Reference and worked answers','<p class="big">Use these after an attempt, or when live access is unavailable.</p><p>Recorded examples belong to the November 13 technical rehearsal. They are not results from your unexecuted changes.</p>'+note('Use the return links to continue the workshop.'),'These pages are optional answers and recorded examples. Open an answer after participants have tried the exercise. Use the return link to get back to the teaching sequence.','', 'REFERENCE')
add('answer-trace','Put the attribute inside the tool scope',code('def instrument_tool(observation):\n    with tracing.Tool(\n        name=observation["name"],\n        arguments=observation["arguments"],\n        result=observation["result"],\n        started_at=stamp(observation["started_at"]),\n        ended_at=stamp(observation["ended_at"]),\n    ) as tool:\n        tool.set_attributes({"workshop.exercise": "solar-research"})\n        if observation.get("error"):\n            tool.record_error(RuntimeError(observation["error"]))'), 'The attribute is attached inside the Tool scope. The complete notebook function also supplies its call identity and outer conversation. Use the operation’s timestamps so Agent Lens shows when the work happened, not when it was uploaded.','answer-code','WORKED ANSWER')
add('answer-persistence','Return a copy of the latest observation',code('def persistence_forecast(split):\n    return split["persistence"].copy()')+'<p>The copy lets you work with the predictions without changing the dataset.</p>', 'The prepared split includes the last observed reading for each forecast window. Return a copy so later changes to the prediction array cannot alter the dataset.','answer-code','WORKED ANSWER')
add('answer-flux','Take the mean of the absolute errors',code('def training_loss(prediction, target, mask):\n    return ((prediction - target).square() * mask).sum() / mask.sum()\n\ndef my_flux_mae(prediction, target):\n    return float(np.abs(prediction - target).mean())\n\nassert my_flux_mae(np.ones(3), np.zeros(3)) == 1.0\nassert my_flux_mae(np.zeros(3), np.zeros(3)) == 0.0'), 'Subtract prediction and target, take absolute values, and average. A prediction of one against a target of zero gives one. These are log10 flux units. The training loss above it is separate and uses squared error.','answer-code','WORKED ANSWER')
add('answer-search','Compare the settings and loss curves', '<p class="big">Open two runs from the Sweep. Compare their model, width, learning rate, and training steps.</p><p>Then open the loss curves. A lower validation error is easier to interpret when you can see how each model trained.</p><div class="bottom-note">If a run failed, inspect its error. A missing score cannot rank that model.</div>', 'Open the configuration and curve for two runs. Find the settings they share and the value that differs. If training failed, inspect the error rather than assigning a score to a forecast that does not exist.','', 'WORKED ANSWER')
add('answer-images','Average the error inside the disk mask',code('def my_image_mae(prediction, target, disk_mask):\n    errors = np.abs(prediction - target) * disk_mask\n    per_image = errors.sum(axis=(1, 2, 3))\n    per_image /= disk_mask.sum(axis=(1, 2, 3))\n    return float(per_image.mean())')+'<p>Test zero error, constant +1 error, and an error only outside the mask.</p>', 'The mask selects the solar disk. Compute the sum and count per image, then average across images. Check identical arrays, a constant one-unit difference, and a difference only outside the mask.','answer-code','WORKED ANSWER')
add('answer-residual','Add the correction to input channel 1',code('def forward(self, x):\n    correction = self.net(x)\n    if architecture == "residual":\n        return x[:, 1:2] + correction\n    return correction')+note('The current image is input channel 1. The return has one channel.'), 'Channel zero is the earlier image and channel one is the current image. Add the correction to channel one. With a zero correction, this function returns the current image exactly.','answer-code','WORKED ANSWER')
add('answer-evidence','Return validation evidence only', code('def select_validation_evidence(record):\n    if record.get("split") != "validation":\n        raise ValueError("Only validation evidence is allowed.")\n    fields = ("split", "config", "metrics", "losses",\n              "errors", "trace", "stage_id", "lessons")\n    return {name: record[name] for name in fields if name in record}')+note('The agent also receives the current source. Keep final predictions and scores out of this request.'), 'First check that the record belongs to validation. Then return only the listed evidence fields. The current source is supplied separately. The final-test example should raise an error before the agent sees it.','', 'WORKED ANSWER')
add('answer-controller','Pass the candidate’s code to training',code('candidate = proposal["candidates"][candidate_index]\nprobe = run_training(\n    session, stage_name, candidate["source"],\n    image_splits, parent["config"], dataset_version, metric_source,\n)')+note('Use the candidate’s source here. Passing the parent would train the old program again.'), "Pass candidate['source'] to training, along with the shared configuration. Passing the parent source here would train the old program while the interface appeared to test a new proposal. Open the saved candidate.py if the result looks suspicious.",'answer-code','WORKED ANSWER')
add('answer-final','Use the saved model without training it again', '<p class="big">Load each selected model’s saved weights and predict the reserved dates.</p><p>Compare the three image forecasts at one timestamp. The input images and observed future should match across all three rows.</p><div class="bottom-note">Persistence copies the current image and needs no trained weights.</div>', 'The selected weights are already trained. Load them and predict the final inputs. Compare the same target timestamps across all versions; persistence uses the current image directly.','', 'WORKED ANSWER')
add('recorded-edit','Round 1: two changes, two measured outcomes', '<table class="clean-table"><tr><th>Source</th><th>Validation error ↓</th></tr><tr><td>Manual residual model</td><td>0.122116</td></tr><tr><td>A · replace squared loss with absolute loss</td><td>0.120553</td></tr><tr><td>B · initialize the residual head at zero</td><td>0.111434</td></tr></table>'+f'<p>The composition selected B. Its separate test reproduced 0.111434.</p><p class="aside"><a href="{TRACE}">Open the actual proposals and evidence ↗</a></p>', 'In our November 13 rehearsal, Candidate A changed the loss to absolute error. Candidate B initialized the residual head at zero and had lower validation error. The composition kept B and its separate test reproduced the same score. These models shared the image data, seed, and forty-step training configuration.', '', 'RECORDED REHEARSAL')
add('recorded-code','Initialize the correction at zero', code("if architecture == 'residual':\n    nn.init.zeros_(self.net[4].weight)\n    nn.init.zeros_(self.net[4].bias)\n\n# The residual forward pass remains:\nreturn prediction + x[:, 1:2]")+note('Zero initial correction → the initial forecast is the current image.'), 'Zero weights and bias in the last convolution make the initial correction zero. The residual model therefore starts by copying the present image, then learns a correction during training. This is the actual first-round edit that was selected in the recorded run.', 'answer-code', 'RECORDED REHEARSAL')
add('recorded-keep','Round 2 also tested the unchanged version', '<table class="clean-table"><tr><th>Source</th><th>Validation error ↓</th></tr><tr><td>Adopted zero-init model</td><td>0.111434</td></tr><tr><td>A · add absolute loss to that source</td><td>0.110916</td></tr><tr><td>B · KEEP the zero-init source unchanged</td><td>0.111434</td></tr></table><p>The unchanged version reproduced its earlier error. The tested composition selected A.</p>'+note('KEEP ran the same code again so we could compare it with Candidate A.'), 'Round two started from the zero-initialized model. Candidate A added absolute training loss. Candidate B kept the source unchanged and reproduced its error. The tested composition selected A. This small validation difference comes from one seed, so it does not establish repeatability.', '', 'RECORDED REHEARSAL')
add('recorded-final','In this rehearsal, image error fell 10.15%', f'<div class="measured-grid"><div><div class="measured-gain">{relative_gain:.2%}</div><p>less error than the manually selected model</p><p class="aside">Agent edits: zero-initialize the residual head, then use absolute training loss.</p></div><table class="clean-table"><tr><th>Frozen version</th><th>Masked MAE ↓</th></tr><tr><td>Persistence</td><td>{image_results["persistence"]["error"]:.6f}</td></tr><tr><td>Manual residual model</td><td>{image_results["manual"]["error"]:.6f}</td></tr><tr><td>Agent-selected code</td><td>{image_results["agent"]["error"]:.6f}</td></tr></table></div><p class="aside">Actual AIA 171 Å observations. 199 overlapping windows; February 13–14, 2014; one seed. <a href="{REPORT}">Open the recorded comparison ↗</a></p>'+note('A measured result from this rehearsal, not a promised outcome for your edits.'), 'The selected agent code combined the zero-initialized residual head from round one with absolute training loss from round two. Its final masked MAE was 0.11001095193834161, versus 0.1224417336622075 for the manual model and 0.12576198700564592 for persistence. The 10.15% is a relative reduction in error versus manual. This is one seed and 199 overlapping windows across two reserved days, not evidence of reliable solar forecasting across other periods.', '', '3:45 · RECORDED REHEARSAL')
add('recorded-image','Compare the saved forecasts at the same time', '<a class="final-crop" href="/images/ux-v020-solar-final.png" target="_blank" aria-label="Open the complete final notebook comparison"><img src="/images/ux-v020-solar-final.png" alt="Actual notebook comparing manual and agent forecasts at the same reserved timestamp, with observed future and error images"></a><div class="image-caption">Same input and future timestamp. Manual above, agent-selected below. <a href="/images/ux-v020-solar-final.png" target="_blank">Full notebook comparison ↗</a></div>', 'These are saved forecasts for the same final timestamp. Compare the manual row with the agent-selected row, including the error images. The full screenshot also contains the score tables. It is the notebook comparison from the rehearsal.', '', 'RECORDED REHEARSAL')
add('recorded-goes','The recorded GOES model lost to persistence',pic('goes-final.png','Recorded observed flux and undertrained forecast','Final log-flux MAE: selected model 2.469; persistence 0.193. The training budget was 60 steps.'),'The GOES model’s final log-flux MAE was 2.469; persistence scored 0.193. Its learning curve showed it was still undertrained after sixty steps. Keep this failure beside the image result. It does not establish that MLPs or CNNs cannot forecast solar measurements.','', 'RECORDED REHEARSAL')
add('recorded-lens','Open the recorded research conversation', f'<p class="big"><a href="{TRACE}">Open the proposal and its recorded tool activity ↗</a></p><p>Find the active configuration, the requested edit, and the returned candidate code. Compare the proposal with the tested source.</p><p class="aside"><a href="https://ash0ts.github.io/forge-workshop-kit/solar/recorded-study.json">Download the recorded source, decisions, scores, and evidence links ↗</a></p>'+note('Agent Lens may require sign-in. The source and saved decisions are also in the downloadable evidence.'), 'Open the proposal conversation and follow the evidence-reading tool to the candidate source. The downloadable records contain the same decisions and scores if the native view requires sign-in.', '', 'RECORDED REHEARSAL')
add('recovery','When a service is unavailable', '<table class="clean-table"><tr><th>Failure</th><th>Next action</th></tr><tr><td>Project authentication or permission</td><td>Fix access, then retry the check</td></tr><tr><td>Training or inference failed</td><td>Inspect the saved error before retrying work</td></tr><tr><td>Trace or artifact upload failed</td><td>Retry export of the saved execution</td></tr><tr><td>Native EvalTables HTTP 500</td><td>Use notebook and Weave comparisons; retry publication</td></tr></table>', 'Start with the failed operation. An authentication problem needs corrected access. A failed training run needs its saved error inspected. An upload failure needs a publication retry. Native EvalTables returned HTTP 500 during this rehearsal; the notebook and Weave comparisons are still available.','', 'REFERENCE')
add('schedule','Four-hour session', '<table class="clean-table schedule"><tr><th>Minutes</th><th>Work</th></tr><tr><td>0–15</td><td>Copy, connect, instrument</td></tr><tr><td>15–40</td><td>Data and persistence</td></tr><tr><td>40–90</td><td>Tracking and six configurations</td></tr><tr><td>90–100</td><td>Break</td></tr><tr><td>100–135</td><td>Image predictors</td></tr><tr><td>135–195</td><td>Evidence and two research rounds</td></tr><tr><td>195–240</td><td>Freeze, compare, reproduce, explain</td></tr></table>', 'Use these times to pace the room. They include coding and discussion, not just execution. If a section takes longer, use its recorded example for discussion rather than claiming a learner’s unexecuted code produced that result.','', 'REFERENCE')
